{\pard\qc\sb120\sa120\b\fs32 Corvane Mutual Insurance Society Limited\par}
{\pard\qc\sa200\fs22 Motor Fleet UK \u8211? Policy Wording \u8211? Edition June 2009\par}
{\pard\sa160\box\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp60\i\fs18 ARCHIVE COPY. Motor Fleet UK was closed to new business in 2015; this wording is retained for reference on run-off claims only.\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 Prepared for claims use by Rob Tennant, Claims Operations Manager \u8211? Leeds. Effective for policies incepting or renewing on or after 1 June 2009.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 1. About this policy\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 This wording, the schedule and any endorsements form one contract. Cover applies to the vehicles named in the fleet schedule and only for the sections the schedule shows as operative.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 2. Definitions\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa80\fs20 \u8226? Fleet schedule: the list of insured vehicles we hold for you, as amended from time to time.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa80\fs20 \u8226? Insured vehicle: any vehicle shown in the fleet schedule.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa80\fs20 \u8226? Excess: the part of each claim that you must pay yourself.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa80\fs20 \u8226? You, your: the policyholder named in the schedule. We, us, our: Corvane Mutual Insurance Society Limited.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 3. Section A \u8211? Loss of or damage to insured vehicles\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 We cover accidental loss of or damage to any insured vehicle, including fire, theft and attempted theft, together with accessories while fitted to the vehicle.\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 We may repair the vehicle, replace it or pay for the loss in cash.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 4. Section B \u8211? Liability to third parties\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 We will cover your legal liability for death of or injury to any person, and for damage to property, arising from the use of an insured vehicle on a road or in a public place.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 5. The excess\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 Under Section A you must pay an excess of \u163?500 per vehicle for each and every claim. Where one incident damages more than one insured vehicle, the excess applies to each vehicle.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 6. General exceptions\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 This policy does not cover any vehicle while it is being driven by a person who does not hold a valid licence to drive it, or who is not permitted to drive it under the schedule.\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 Wear and tear, mechanical or electrical breakdown and loss of use are not covered.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 7. Claims conditions\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 Tell us as soon as possible about any incident that may lead to a claim, and send us any letter, claim form or legal document unanswered.\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 You must not admit liability or offer to settle any claim without our written agreement.\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa80\b\fs24 8. Cancellation\par}
{\pard\sa120\fs20 You or we may cancel this policy by giving written notice. Any refund of premium is set out in the schedule.\par}
